Read [the stack](/docs/the-stack/) for the composition. Install the
toolchain on [Install](/docs/install/) if this machine is new.

## What does the code feel like?

A component is a PascalCase `@component` that lowers to a pure Roc function
returning `Html`. This `Hello` is from the cataloged styling example:

```rocci
@component
Hello = |{ name ?? "Roc" }| {
    @css {
        .greeting {
            margin: 0;
            color: #c9d8d2;
        }
    }
    <p class="greeting">Hello, <strong>{name}</strong></p>
}
```

Preview it after [install](/docs/install/):

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- view \
  examples/rocci/standalone/styling/Styling.rocci \
  --component Hello --arg name=Ada
```

Complete source: [Styling.rocci](/examples/styling/source/Styling-rocci/).

